  "Question": "Six rectangles each with a common base width of \\(2\\) have lengths of \\(1,\\) \\(4,\\) \\(9,\\) \\(16,\\) \\(25,\\) and \\(36.\\) What is the sum of the areas of the six rectangles?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\( 91 \\)",
    "B": "\\( 93 \\)",
    "C": "\\( 162 \\)",
    "D": "\\( 182 \\)",
    "E": "\\( 202 \\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "A rectangle's area is its length times its width. Since every rectangle has width \\(2\\), we can add the lengths first and then multiply by \\(2\\):\n\\[\n2(1+4+9+16+25+36)=2\\times91=182.\n\\]\nThe sum of the areas is \\(182\\) square units, choice \\(\\mathrm{D}\\).",
